An `Error` carries a message and an unsigned numeric code.

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    missing = Error("Missing value")
    coded = Error("Missing value", 200)
]

The code defaults to `0` and accepts `0` through `4294967295`. A negative code is
rejected, and an `I32` variable needs an explicit fallible conversion.

Use the message to explain the failure. Use the code when a stable category is
useful to callers or tools.

Code `0` does not mean success when a function returns the value as an error.
Under the accepted contract, a bound catch for implicit numeric failure also
receives `Error`. Typed errors keep their original message and code when caught.

The Progress matrix owns current backend support: @../progress (Progress).
